# Action Loading UX

User-triggered actions (buttons, submits):

## 1. Loading on active button

- Spinner: `Loader2` + `className="animate-spin"`
- Button text: progress label (`Saving...`, `Sending...`, `Deleting...`)

```tsx
<Button disabled={isBusy}>
  {busyKey === "save-item" ? (
    <>
      <Loader2 className="animate-spin" aria-hidden />
      Saving...
    </>
  ) : (
    "Save"
  )}
</Button>
```

## 2. Block peers until done/fail

- Shared `busyKey` / `isBusy` while async runs
- Disable related inputs/checkboxes/buttons in same panel when `isBusy`
- Re-enable in `finally`

```tsx
const isBusy = busyKey !== null;

<Input disabled={isBusy} />
<Button disabled={isBusy}>Submit</Button>
```

## 3. Checklist

- [ ] Set `busyKey` at async start
- [ ] Clear `busyKey` in `finally`
- [ ] Disable actionable elements when busy
- [ ] Spinner + loading text on trigger button
- [ ] `aria-hidden` on decorative spinners

## 4. Results via toast

- `notify` from `@/lib/notify` for success/error
- `notify.success(message)` / `notify.error(message)`
- No inline message divs / per-component feedback state

```tsx
import { notify } from "@/lib/notify";

// On success
notify.success("User roles updated.");

// On error
notify.error(error.message ?? "Something went wrong.");
```
